Third-party software and models this project builds on:

1. Shap-E (OpenAI)
   https://github.com/openai/shap-e
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 OpenAI.
   The Python check/export tooling in shap_e/src/cli uses the upstream Shap-E
   PyTorch implementation as the reference oracle and to obtain the original
   checkpoints for conversion. The MLX (Python) and ShapERuntime (Swift)
   implementations in this repository are ports of that model architecture.

2. CLIP (OpenAI)
   https://github.com/openai/CLIP
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 OpenAI.
   Shap-E conditions on CLIP-ViT-L/14 embeddings. The BPE vocabulary file
   (bpe_simple_vocab_16e6.txt.gz) expected by the Swift tokenizer comes from
   the CLIP project. It is not included in this repository; obtain it from
   the CLIP project.

3. TripoSR (Tripo AI & Stability AI / VAST-AI-Research)
   https://github.com/VAST-AI-Research/TripoSR
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 Tripo AI & Stability AI.
   Included as the TripoSR git submodule, which carries its own LICENSE. The
   Swift port under TripoSR/swift is part of that submodule.

4. MLX and mlx-swift (Apple)
   https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx
   https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-swift
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Apple Inc.
   Used as ordinary package dependencies (SwiftPM / PyPI); not vendored.

Model weights:
No pretrained model weights are included in this repository. Converted
weights (runtime_bundle/) and downloaded checkpoints (shap_e_model_cache/)
are git-ignored local artifacts that each user must generate or download
under the upstream projects' licenses. The only tensors checked in are the
tiny random-weight test stub under
shap_e/swift/Tests/ShapERuntimeTests/Fixtures/, which contains no trained
parameters.
